{"title":"2017 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Omega_Learn)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Omega Learn)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(WhyMath)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (WhyMath)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For any positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, the notation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/d/32dca76f56a772e66047d31d3eed93862b634710.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" /> denotes the product of the integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> through\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />. What is the largest integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/2/5b216498b4cb64f29f3bfdfa60736dc769f06c7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is a factor of the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/b/a4bb24c721245d75bc4dbbdc549a21f8bff00291.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$98!+99!+100!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"125\" height=\"16\" />&#160;?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/8/508919234f7d7d4610fcbda7020247cd655380e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }23 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }24 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) }25 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) }26 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) }27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"401\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Factoring out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/b/a4bb24c721245d75bc4dbbdc549a21f8bff00291.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$98!+99!+100!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"125\" height=\"16\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/6/5d62d4fa4b09644b6311603f0017c08c5e6eaf69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$98! (1+99+99\\cdot100)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"170\" height=\"20\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/6/516764ff7d637934a3268082ed0b435ef123cd07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$98! (10000)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"85\" height=\"20\" />. Next, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/6/046283a0339c09c897ff0130a30982333039fdd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$98!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/5/fc5aa89f49e531c842e3434aae1fe18706fcfa44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor\\frac{98}{5}\\right\\rfloor + \\left\\lfloor\\frac{98}{25}\\right\\rfloor = 19 + 3 = 22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"226\" height=\"45\" /> factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is because of all the multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is because of all the multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Now, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/b/50b19142d92b7b4f1a115c4ec91766582e2b8faf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10,000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"17\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so there are a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/4/d3411502928ef134224d654573f0ae95d27d6a8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22 + 4 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 26}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"140\" height=\"30\" /> factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~CHECKMATE2021\n</p><p>Note: Do you know what formula this uses? Most AMC 8 test takers won't know it. \nIt's <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Legendre%27s_Formula\" title=\"Legendre&#39;s Formula\">Legendre's Formula</a>.\n</p><p>～ a quick note if not prefer formula: \nFactor out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/6/046283a0339c09c897ff0130a30982333039fdd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$98!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/d/c8d277285d37b04a2a296a54a9a75d0a8600cbc3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[98! + 99! + 100! = 98!\\,(1 + 99 + 99\\cdot 100) = 98! \\cdot 10000.\\]\" width=\"426\" height=\"18\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/8/a0817bef8a605824bc260363414344bcd16adf89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10000 = 10^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"97\" height=\"17\" /> contains four factors of 5, it contributes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/d/c5df324769ac1365d3b379a13a1f21c3333e9952.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^4$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />.\nTo count the factors of 5 in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/6/046283a0339c09c897ff0130a30982333039fdd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$98!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" />, count multiples of 5 and then add the extra factor from each multiple of 25: there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> multiples of 5 (from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/1/0510fa96a9909623c5966ad29945fabc84c704a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$95$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />) and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> multiples of 25 (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/7/d0777200800c3b382dc2d591a61d2cea8cbda529.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25, 50, 75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"17\" />), while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/8/e283119f60ea90639ce1dbca39a4c3703c7aaa69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$125 &gt; 98$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"15\" /> adds nothing. This gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/3/b43c762149153f1e701a5e5837c9ee011f6b3b5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19 + 3 = 22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" /> factors of 5.\nTherefore the largest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/d/b5d11a57ab77748e22ca9ba7f53fc0e17c048255.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22 + 4 = 26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/5/2a51c21d979ab90fc16ff035d49956d27b9ffdea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 26}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Omega_Learn.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Omega_Learn)\">Video Solution (Omega Learn)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Omega Learn)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HISL2-N5NVg&amp;t=817s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HISL2-N5NVg&amp;t=817s</a>\n</p><p>~ GeometryMystery\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28WhyMath.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(WhyMath)\">Video Solution (WhyMath)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (WhyMath)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/meEuDzrM5Ac\">https://youtu.be/meEuDzrM5Ac</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margi